deflate/inflate: one shared, named version string

Kind: link-composition stand-in (the bytes come from an object this build
does not link).

The reference keeps "1.1.3" at 0x1002706c, directly after broadcast.obj's
literals, and deflateInit2_'s static my_version pointer after it at
0x10027074; every ZLIB_VERSION user in the image shares that one
address. /O2 implies /Gf, so stock sources already share one pooled literal
COMDAT, and only its position is wrong: stock deflate.obj emits the pointer
before the literal (17 bytes differ). Linking stock compress.c, the first
object in link order whose code (compress2) references ZLIB_VERSION, puts
the literal exactly at 0x1002706c from compress.obj; the TL client links
compress.c. This build leaves compress.c out because it would add a game C
object to the Rich header (docs/msvc6-link-layout.md 5f) and moves the stock
CRT load order. Until the composition admits compress.obj, a named array
defined before the pointer gives the same 12 bytes. vfs.c references the
array as g_zlib_version.

--- a/deflate.c
+++ b/deflate.c
@@ -51,6 +51,9 @@
 
 #include "deflate.h"
 
+/* Shared writable version string, preceding the static version pointer. */
+char g_zlib_version[] = ZLIB_VERSION;
+
 const char deflate_copyright[] =
    " deflate 1.1.3 Copyright 1995-1998 Jean-loup Gailly ";
 /*
@@ -212,7 +215,7 @@
 {
     deflate_state *s;
     int noheader = 0;
-    static const char* my_version = ZLIB_VERSION;
+    static const char* my_version = g_zlib_version;
 
     ushf *overlay;
     /* We overlay pending_buf and d_buf+l_buf. This works since the average
--- a/inflate.c
